<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>#(title)</title>
</head>

<body>
  <h1>#(title)</h1>

  <div id="story"></div>

  <p>You are awoken roughly by the echoing and vibrations of distant drums that shake the stone walls you call yours. Every item in your cell is affected by the intense noise, from the standard issue half-broken toothbrush to the dented cup it rests in. You can hear the distant roar of hundreds of thousands, clamoring and eagerly anticipating the day's events. You were one of them once, as you fondly remember going to Prima Noxa as a kid. The food, the fanfare, and the games were the stuff of recent legend, and you naively wished to be a part of it then.</p>
  <p>Your good thoughts are quickly scattered as a guard bangs on the front bars, screaming at you to get ready. The guard cuffs you and takes you down the cold and imperialistic corridors where the others are housed, while every second the drums and the crowd get louder and louder, and the anxious pit in your stomach grows. Flags of fallen empires drape the lowly walls, hanging as trophies of once-known places. Most tattered, some sun-bleached. They must have come a long way, you think to yourself. You are thirsty, hungry, and angry. Each step feels like a chore, as the soreness feels like it is seeping through your muscles and all the way to your bones.</p>
  <p>"Special fight today. They got the last batch of Ganinite prisoners escorted out of the front lines, and boy, are some of them mad," you overhear as your guard's communication relay is turned up too loud. Great, you think to yourself. The last remnants of a dying empire specially shipped out just to fight in one of the largest events of the year, no wonder they are mad. They really couldn't just get normal prisoners for your second fight ever, huh.</p>
  <p>The guard escorting you is in full riot gear, with a curved light rifle pointed right at your kidneys. The brushed metal seems to blend in with the red and gray of the walls, as the corridor widens and the flags turn from other empires to yours. You despise the crimson, as it represents the worst and the last things that many worlds, and many people, have seen.</p>
  <p>"And STOP. Now it's time for the second worst part of your day today. Paperwork," the guard grunts at you, as you can barely hear him over the sound of the steps and shouts of potentially millions of people directly above you.</p>

  <form action="/create-character" method="POST">
    <label for="characterName">Name:</label>
    <input type="text" id="characterName" name="characterName" required>
    <br>

    <label for="characterGender">Gender:</label>
    <select id="characterGender" name="characterGender">
      <option value="male">Male</option>
      <option value="female">Female</option>
      <option value="other">Other</option>
    </select>
    <br>

    <label for="fightingSpecialty">Fighting Specialty:</label>
    <select id="fightingSpecialty" name="fightingSpecialty" required>
      <option value="sheer strength">Sheer strength</option>
      <option value="technique">Technique</option>
      <option value="agility">Agility</option>
    </select>
    <br>

    <label for="armorClass">Armor Class:</label>
    <select id="armorClass" name="armorClass" required>
      <option value="heavy">Heavy</option>
      <option value="medium">Medium</option>
      <option value="light">Light</option>
    </select>
    <br>

    <label for="homePlanet">Home Planet:</label>
    <input type="text" id="homePlanet" name="homePlanet" required>
    <br>

    <input type="submit" value="Give paperwork">
  </form>
</body>
</html>